<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρα-ζεύγνυμι</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρα-ύω</span></b> , aor. 2
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεζύγην [ῠ</span>] <i><span class="en">
			Epicur.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			59
		</span></i>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>yoke
				beside, couple</i> in marriage, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστῷ πονηρὸν λέκτρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					520
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρουρὼ π. φύλακε σώματος</span>
			<i>having set beside</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ion</u>
				22
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be coupled to</i> another, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνὴ ἐσθλὴ παραζευχθεῖσα καὶ σῴζει
					δόμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1055.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
			</span></i> l.c.: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				D.
				<u>Prooem.</u>
				55
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>associate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.71
				</span></i>
			 K.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be associated</i> in a task, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRyl.</u>
				237.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ παρεζευγμένη
				χωλεία</span> the <i>associated</i> lameness, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.Cit.
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
